  "failure_resolution": [
    "Initial baseline had two fixture errors: Short Bow costs {2}, so full Convoke/Delve controls need two contributors/fuel; Delve requires an already-present provider. Corrected baseline is retained separately.",
    "An inherited private CostContext literal needed mana_closed:false; all legacy constructors now compile.",
    "An inherited Kili test activated Bolg inside a final-zero equip announcement. It now uses actual Skyseer's Chariot naming My Precious to impose tax {2}, making a legal mana window while still proving the locked free equip alternative survives sacrificing its provider. Life remains 20; the generated black/red mana pays the tax.",
    "One additional-bound selection used a filename prefix instead of its module filter and reported zero selected tests. Corrected module selection passes 7/7; both reports retained."
  ],
  "ownership_privacy_transaction": [
    "Zero acknowledgment and already-funded nonmana-first payment use raw/index/restore after parent disposal; wrong actors and forbidden mana actions reject without state mutation.",
    "No new public state, actions, serialization fields or wire schema. The existing public mana_closed state is only retained in private ephemeral query context; private memo identity now distinguishes it.",
    "The stranded remaining-cost scenario deliberately removes pooled mana in an owned test fork to verify its proposal cannot invent a forbidden late mana child. It is not claimed as an independently reachable public payment sequence.",
    "Dracogenesis keeps its exact immutable physical identity under a scoped typed provider fixture; native Shivan Dragon is cast through the existing filtered free permission. No gated definition is admitted."
  ],
